{"conversation_id":"f365ef1d-caa2-4379-8e96-51e64ca36af8","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Completed the owner-directed refactor moving the guest-agnostic execution-host specification and the canonical service ABI tables into [`docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md), renaming the service ABI `yin.register.host.v1` → `yin.vm.engine.host.v1` across all design documents with dated `2026-10-19` owner-ruling notes, slimming [`docs/design/yin.vm.register-wasm.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.register-wasm.md) to the register-machine instance, and updating [`docs/design/yang.wasm.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.wasm.md), [`docs/design/yin.vm.conformance-kit.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.conformance-kit.md), and [`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md). No files in `src/` or `test/` were touched, and lines `1–1334` of `yin.vm.rust-kernel.md` did not shift.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Files Written / Updated\n\n1. **Amended [`docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md)** — added dated `2026-10-19` correction notes for `:store-updates` → `:resource-updates` / `:resources` (`{:rule :resource-update-key}`) in the existing body (`§1.1`, `§2.1`, `§3`) and appended the design-only extension `## Extension (2026-10-19, design only): the engine execution host for guest machines` (`§E.1–§E.5`).\n2. **Updated [`docs/design/yang.wasm.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.wasm.md)** — renamed the target ABI to `yin.vm.engine.host.v1` with a dated `2026-10-19` owner-ruling note, replaced inline ABI tables in `§4` with references to [`yin.vm.engine.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md) `§E.3`, and updated guest-agnostic host references to `yin.vm.engine.md` `§E.1–§E.5`.\n3. **Slimmed [`docs/design/yin.vm.register-wasm.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.register-wasm.md)** — retained only the register-machine instance (`§1` eight materialized register fields and sync-barrier instance, `§2` sparse continuations and `register-restore`, `§3` register module attachment and `spawn-module`, `§4` register-specific W0–W6 gates, `§5` register-specific risks/conventions/open items), renamed the ABI to `yin.vm.engine.host.v1`, and cross-linked [`yin.vm.engine.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md) `§E.1–§E.5`.\n4. **Updated [`docs/design/yin.vm.conformance-kit.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.conformance-kit.md)** — renamed the ABI to `yin.vm.engine.host.v1` with a dated `2026-10-19` owner-ruling note and updated guest-agnostic host/protocol/traversal citations to [`yin.vm.engine.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md) `§E.1–§E.5`.\n5. **Updated [`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md)** — updated `line 1300` in-place and `lines 1335–1338` to cite [`yin.vm.engine.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md) (`§E.1–§E.5`, `yin.vm.engine.host.v1`) and record the `2026-10-19` owner ruling without shifting lines `1–1334`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. [`docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md) Extension Section List \u0026 Body Corrections\n\n- **Body `:store-updates` → `:resource-updates` corrections (dated `2026-10-19`)**:\n  - Top header note (`lines 7–11`): records the `2026-10-19` correction across `§1.1`, `§2.1`, and `§3`.\n  - `### 1.1 Names and the program store (Rule R)` (`lines 73–77`): updated `resume-from-run-queue` prose to `:resource-updates` merged into private `:resources`, refusing non-keyword keys with `{:rule :resource-update-key}` (noting historical `:store-updates` / `{:rule :store-update-key}`).\n  - `### 2.1 The restore function` (`lines 143–146`): updated `base` description to `:resource-updates` merged into `:resources`.\n  - `## 3. The entry key contract` (`lines 193–198`): updated engine-owned key list to `:resource-updates` with a dated `2026-10-19` correction note.\n- **Design-Only Extension (`lines 360–924`)**:\n  - `## Extension (2026-10-19, design only): the engine execution host for guest machines` (Status, `2026-10-18` r5 consensus provenance, `2026-10-19` owner ruling and decomposition notes, Authorities and companion specifications)\n  - `### E.1 The machine-state-as-data boundary and synchronization protocol` (`lines 405–467`)\n  - `### E.2 The value arena, handle discipline, and three encoding domains` (`lines 469–607`)\n    - `#### E.2.1 Task-owned value arena, i32 handles, and the native handle↔Value facade`\n    - `#### E.2.2 Three encoding domains and mandatory native hashing`\n    - `#### E.2.3 Arena collection, GC root discipline, and snapshot isolation`\n  - `### E.3 Service protocol: yin.vm.engine.host.v1` (`lines 609–757`)\n    - `#### E.3.1 Offsets and ownership` (including the canonical control-offset table `+0` through `+60`)\n    - `#### E.3.2 Transport status values, execution statuses, and once-only response delivery`\n    - `#### E.3.3 Plain-data TLV encoding, canonical ordering, and Float64/NaN rules` (including the canonical Tag `0–13` table)\n    - `#### E.3.4 Message envelope, task-local references, and required operations`\n  - `### E.4 The embedder seam, single-engine-port rule, and deterministic traversal` (`lines 759–872`)\n    - `#### E.4.1 Host responsibilities, embedder targets, and IVM step/run contract`\n    - `#### E.4.2 Single-engine-port rule, fault containment, and Rust-kernel reconciliations`\n    - `#### E.4.3 Deterministic service traversal prerequisite` (including the 7-row `engine.cljc`/`module.cljc` traversal table)\n    - `#### E.4.4 Stream, park, custody-gate, F